hod":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-60-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5058016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3928027589caff0686a88391eda521baeaf7cc962efbb23c0366312b48b99f03","compact":"2f26d5a7591c2b49021b9225b50c2ea361ff2a280bf67c2059290bd49cf503d6","nasal":"d178b5ebee41aa71daeec3d7edc8c50e33daf0db069e2687486c3bb453060f71"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-58-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":58,"verse":17,"english":"The monkey-chief Sugrīva's maternal uncle, the heroic and high-souled Dadhimukha always guard that picturesque and spacious garden of the lord of monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.486,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5058017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e6ebc85201bf2bc3a0e3f58953b3cf47aea58d8ee2b6e2091e15f7c4c7bf98fc","compact":"d40e73d36d50790110c5563792bd9120a7296d076604ccaab9aacc51e342f87e","nasal":"2afcb080412d77b03d830ffdcc07a86085094dce24a9b72087cfd78e93414d58"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-58-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":58,"verse":18,"english":"I have heard, that, by Wind-god's son alone Lankā was burnt. You are all famed for your manliness, it dose not behove you to speak before Rāma. “We have seen the worshipful dame but have not been able to bring her.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.607,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-60-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5058018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33504f38a6dce72975bbe380049dc566c5d84119dd9fa3fe0c77e8676c3590cb","compact":"da31d9d5d2c1c7b4e6ce721fc45cb7f17c2f03f29ad3279108e50ad247f25eda","nasal":"da31d9d5d2c1c7b4e6ce721fc45cb7f17c2f03f29ad3279108e50ad247f25eda"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-58-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":58,"verse":19,"english":"You foremost of monkeys, there is none among the celestials or Asuras who can equal you either in leaping or in prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-60-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5058019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"839e1c30d09c406847f44447f67b43ad7039b74614b13f79602642e1d9d8582e","compact":"b234c91975999c2353ee7284a61d506a6d30d96cbb4087b89c509e4633fd98c6","nasal":"adc9b855abc6505e096975b24404f85da2fffc972117cae4349d8379090bedb8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-58-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":58,"verse":20,"english":"What else is there for us to perforin than brining the daughter of the king Janaka when the Rākşasa crew shall be slain by Hanumān?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-60-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5058020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7c0b6876594cc0ec1e17fdf12ded4596112cd6a950311215caa788ec79479436","compact":"705a88ea91dc087024776f7a979b4b50d4971d59aecbe267b696d1c36bf0ba32","nasal":"705a88ea91dc087024776f7a979b4b50d4971d59aecbe267b696d1c36bf0ba32"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-58-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":58,"verse":21,"english":"Thereupon Jāmbavāna, the foremost of the monkeys, greatly delighted spoke to Angada, who was thus resolved, the following pregnant words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-60-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5058021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0935a1672bf69d625c6a27c5a6adbf2dec5d27b7b11b57c0c10554abbc3277d1","compact":"667223f2be3d48248659e6fab9ac5551f874c96fd3cc68216edbe7888f90c41c","nasal":"d8fd49a6